CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: a non-virtual destructor of a class template shall not
be implicitly instantiated unless odr-used.  No S<int> object is created here
(only the static member sval() is used), so ~S() is never odr-used and under
lazy instantiation its assertion "must never appear" does not enter the goto
program; the forbidden pattern must be absent.

This became CORE once the special members were deferred.  Destructor odr-use
for automatic/temporary objects is recovered in typecheck_method_bodies() from
the set of constructed classes ([class.dtor]/12): a destructor is instantiated
exactly when its class is constructed, so this static-only case (no object,
hence no constructor odr-used) correctly leaves ~S() uninstantiated.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md §13.
